# elevator: elevator simulation in Python (Poisson arrivals, three dispatch strategies, metrics, CSV).
# Components, globs, exclusions, relations and anchored rules. Anchors come after the period.

# --- components and the files that implement them
The program "elevator" contains the module "cli", the module "text_output", the module "csv_output", the module "execution", the module "simulator", the module "elevator", the module "dispatch", the module "passengers", the module "metrics", the module "config" and the test suite "tests".
The module "cli" is implemented in "elevator/{__init__,__main__,cli}.py".
The module "text_output" is implemented in "elevator/{report,timeline}.py".
The module "csv_output" is implemented in "elevator/output.py".
The module "execution" is implemented in "elevator/execution.py".
The module "simulator" is implemented in "elevator/{simulator,events}.py".
The module "elevator" is implemented in "elevator/elevator.py".
The module "dispatch" is implemented in "elevator/dispatch.py".
The module "passengers" is implemented in "elevator/passengers.py".
The module "metrics" is implemented in "elevator/metrics.py".
The module "config" is implemented in "elevator/config.py".
The test suite "tests" is implemented in "tests/**".
# the .gitignore is not code
The program "elevator" excludes ".gitignore".

# what each module holds and the rules below cite
The module "passengers" contains the random generator "per-floor rng".
The module "simulator" contains the priority queue "EventQueue".
The module "dispatch" contains the registry "STRATEGIES".
The registry "STRATEGIES" contains the strategy "nearest", the strategy "round_robin" and the strategy "zone".

# --- relations
The module "cli" uses the module "dispatch", the module "execution", the module "metrics", the module "text_output", the module "csv_output" and the module "config".
The module "execution" uses the module "simulator", the module "dispatch" and the module "passengers".
The module "simulator" uses the module "elevator".
The module "dispatch" uses the module "elevator".
The module "config" reads the json document "config.json".
The module "csv_output" writes the csv file "output.csv".
The test suite "tests" uses the module "cli", the module "text_output", the module "execution", the module "simulator", the module "elevator", the module "dispatch", the module "passengers", the module "metrics" and the module "config".

# --- layers (each layer sits above the next)
The layer "interface" is above the layer "execution".
The layer "execution" is above the layer "domain".
The layer "domain" is above the layer "data".
The layer "data" is above the layer "external".
The module "cli" is in the layer "interface".
The module "text_output" is in the layer "interface".
The module "csv_output" is in the layer "interface".
The module "execution" is in the layer "execution".
The module "simulator" is in the layer "domain".
The module "elevator" is in the layer "domain".
The module "dispatch" is in the layer "domain".
The module "passengers" is in the layer "domain".
The module "metrics" is in the layer "domain".
The module "config" is in the layer "data".
The json document "config.json" is in the layer "external".
The csv file "output.csv" is in the layer "external".

# --- rules (anchored)
# ties at the same instant are broken by scheduling order: deterministic simulation
The priority queue "EventQueue" is ordered by the value "simulated time". ^elevator/events.py#EventQueue
The priority queue "EventQueue" breaks ties by the value "scheduling order". ^elevator/events.py#EventQueue
The module "simulator" is deterministic. ^elevator/events.py#EventQueue
# an unserved passenger at the end aborts the simulation
If the value "completed passengers" is not the value "generated passengers", the module "simulator" raises the error "RuntimeError". ^elevator/simulator.py#Simulator
# round robin keeps state between calls
The strategy "round_robin" is stateful. ^elevator/dispatch.py#create_round_robin
# every strategy picks among the candidates for a floor call; with no candidate, None
Every strategy in the registry "STRATEGIES" receives the value "floor" and the list "candidates".
Every strategy in the registry "STRATEGIES" returns the record "Elevator" and the value "None".
# per-floor seed: changing the floor count changes the whole list
When the field "floors" changes, the random generator "per-floor rng" changes the list "passengers". ^elevator/passengers.py#generate
The field "floors" is at least 2.
The random generator "per-floor rng" is seeded with the field "seed" and the value "origin floor".
The field "seed" has no limit.
# the timeline has symbols for up to 36 floors; above that it prints ?
If the field "floors" is greater than 36, the module "text_output" prints the value "?". ^elevator/timeline.py#_symbol

# declared view: the contract of the dispatch strategies
The view "strategy contract" shows the registry "STRATEGIES".
The view "strategy contract" shows every "strategy".
The view "strategy contract" shows the record "Elevator", the list "candidates" and the value "floor".
The view "strategy contract" has the form "matrix".
